  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5139",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is shown to interact with P2X purinoceptors, a family of ionotropic receptors that mediate cellular signaling through purine ligand binding. This interaction is supported by a shared target of [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which is a known inhibitor of P2X receptors. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N may act as a modulator of P2X receptors, potentially influencing cellular processes in SK-N-DZ cells, a human neuroendocrine tumor cell line. The consistent pathway from Mollicellin N to SK-N-DZ through P2X receptors indicates a mechanistic link, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of a common inhibitor in all three paths supports a potential role for Mollicellin N in targeting P2X receptors, which could have implications for therapeutic applications in diseases involving these receptors.",
